# Lab 01 — Active Directory Domain Services Setup

In depth tutorial from EastCharmer: https://youtu.be/GsmJowwIh8Q?si=VkQHgoOXbBjTZdtS

## Objective

Build a basic Active Directory environment using a Windows Server virtual
machine and establish an initial organizational structure for managing users,
computers, servers, and groups.

This lab covers:

- Creating a Windows Server virtual machine
- Installing Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)
- Promoting the server to a Domain Controller
- Creating an Organizational Unit (OU) hierarchy
- Creating Active Directory groups
- Understanding group scope and group type
- Creating and organizing user accounts

---

## Lab Environment

### Hypervisor
VMware Workstation Pro

### Server
Windows Server running as a virtual machine

### Server Role
Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)

### Initial AD Structure

The environment is organized geographically using three primary OUs:

```text
Domain
│
├── USA
│   ├── Users
│   ├── Computers
